{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790423939,"nonce":"+YRQmAWkI/3LYdZ8cgpfy8y0CVw=","message":"Stage 1 landed in 2538c0a.\n\n- `aot_runtime` feature (no JIT; `aot` implies it) gates the AOT entry points in capi.rs and the runtime helpers; helpers are no_mangle on wasm32 under it. IC native/host slots now cast through usize so the 4-byte fn pointers transmute on wasm32.\n- JIT-only names split into `JIT_ONLY_FN_NAMES` (host): wren_tier_tick, wren_retier, wren_cold_loop_hot, wren_deopt_n, wren_deopt_at, wren_current_shadow_roots_ptr. `RUNTIME_FN_NAMES` plus `capi::AOT_ENTRY_NAMES` is now exactly what a program's runtime must export.\n- `tools/build_wasm_runtime.sh` builds the staticlib and prelinks with rust-lld -r plus wasi-libc into target/\u003cprofile\u003e/wasm32-wasip1/wlift_runtime.o. Undefined symbols left: WASI preview1 imports and linker-synthesised globals only.\n- `tests/wasm_runtime_fresh.rs` reads the object's linking symbol table; checked against a one-symbol object that it fails naming wlift_aot_new_vm. CI runs clippy for the config, builds the object and runs the test on Linux.\n- Hand check: a C main calling wlift_aot_new_vm + wrenInterpret, linked with the object by rust-lld, runs under wasmtime (classes, loop, fiber yield all correct).\n\nOpen for later stages:\n- krio paths stay host-only (wlift_aot_new_vm's krio_fiber_active, the krio fast path in the fiber call helper); compiled-body fibers are c079735 / stage 6.\n- `wlift_safepoint_page` is host-only (stw.rs, page protection). A wasm program must not import it; stage 3 decides the wasm loop-header poll (none, or a flag load).","files":null}]}